{
  "summary": "Add a constructor to `CTransaction` accepting `std::vector<CTxIn>`, `std::vector<CTxOut>`, and optional version and locktime values, forwarding existing `CMutableTransaction` constructors to it. Add an optional `CScriptWitness` parameter to `CTxIn` constructors to allow direct witness initialization, and adapt unit tests in `sigopcount_tests` to demonstrate declarative immutable transaction construction.",
  "problem": "Constructing an immutable `CTransaction` currently requires instantiating an intermediate `CMutableTransaction`, populating its fields, and converting it. In tests and fixtures, this produces repetitive boilerplate and prevents inline, declarative instantiation of test transactions.",
  "evidence": [
    "Part of #36692 ('Declarative construction of test data')",
    "Commit message: 'CTransaction: Add a value constructor' and PR description: 'CTransaction gains a constructor that allows direct declarative construction as an alternative to building through CMutableTransaction.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": [
      "#36692"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "",
  "changed_since_previous": "Replaced the templated range-based constructor and `RangeOf`/`ToVector` utilities with a concrete constructor taking `std::vector<CTxIn>` and `std::vector<CTxOut>` by value.",
  "card": "CTransaction gains a value constructor taking vectors of inputs and outputs along with optional version and locktime, and CTxIn constructors gain an optional script witness argument. This enables declarative construction of immutable transactions without creating and mutating an intermediate CMutableTransaction. The change is part of issue #36692 to simplify test data setup.",
